{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ומן העפר אשר יהיה בקרקע המשכן", :translit "u'min ha'afar asher yihyeh b'karkat ha'mishkan", :gloss "and from the dust that will be on the floor of the Tabernacle"} {:he "בירושלמי למה מים ועפר", :translit "b'Yerushalmi lama mayim v'afar", :gloss "in the Yerushalmi, why water and dust"} {:he "מים ממקום שבאת עפר למקום שהולכת", :translit "mayim mi'mekom she'bat afar la'mekom she'holechet", :gloss "water from the place she came, dust to the place she goes"} {:he "וכתב שהיא עתידה ליתן דין וחשבון", :translit "v'katav she'hi atidah laten din v'cheshbon", :gloss "and it is written that she is destined to give an accounting"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Water symbolizes birth (amniotic fluid/waters), dust symbolizes death (grave dust)"}], :frame {:text "The Yerushalmi explains the sotah ritual: water represents the amniotic waters from which she emerged at birth, and dust represents the earth of the grave to which she returns. If guilty, she must give a final accounting before God. The pairing of water and dust as bookends of human existence echoes Genesis 18:27, where Abraham describes himself as 'dust and ashes,' and Ecclesiastes 3:20, 'all are from the dust and all return to the dust.' The phrase 'din v'cheshbon' (reckoning and account) is a known rabbinic idiom for divine post-mortem judgment.", :sources ["Yerushalmi Sotah 1:4" "Genesis 18:27" "Ecclesiastes 3:20"]}} {:quotes [{:he "בקרקע", :translit "b'karkat", :gloss "on the floor"} {:he "ב' במסורה", :translit "bet b'masorah", :gloss "twice in the Masorah"} {:he "ואם יסתרו מנגד עיני בקרקע הים", :translit "v'im yistaru mi'neged einai b'karkat ha'yam", :gloss "and if they are hidden from before my eyes in the floor of the sea"} {:he "ואם יסתרו מנגד עיני", :translit "v'im yistaru mi'neged einai", :gloss "and if they are hidden from before my eyes"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["בקרקע המשכן" "בקרקע הים"]} {:kind :other, :note "Reads Job 38:16 phrase as a remez to the sotah ritual: 'hidden from eyes' = suspected wife; 'floor of the sea' = dust and water test"}], :frame {:text "The phrase בקרקע appears exactly twice in Scripture: here in Numbers 5:17 and in Job 38:16, 'Have you entered into the springs of the sea, or walked in the recesses of the deep?' The Ba'al HaTurim reads the Job verse as a veiled allusion to the sotah: the woman 'hidden from the eyes' of her husband is tested through 'the floor of the sea,' i.e., dust and water.", :sources ["Job 38:16" "Numbers 5:17"]}} {:quotes [{:he "בקרקע המשכן", :translit "b'karkat ha'mishkan", :gloss "on the floor of the Tabernacle"} {:he "עי״ן מידלי", :translit "ayin midali", :gloss "ayin is elevated/enlarged"} {:he "כי עין נואף שמרה נשף", :translit "ki ayin no'ef shomrah neshef", :gloss "for the eye of an adulterer watches for twilight"} {:he "לא תשורני עין", :translit "lo t'surani ayin", :gloss "let no eye see me"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Enlarged letter ע in the word בקרקע signals the concealment-seeking 'eye' (עין) of adultery"}], :frame {:text "An enlarged ע in בקרקע alludes to Job 24:15, 'The eye also of the adulterer waits for twilight, saying, Let no eye see me.' The oversized letter thus signals the very crime the sotah ritual investigates: furtive adultery committed under cover of darkness.", :sources ["Job 24:15"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Water symbolizes birth (amniotic fluid/waters), dust symbolizes death (grave dust)", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["בקרקע המשכן" "בקרקע הים"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "בקרקע המשכן", :refs ["Numbers 5:17"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "בקרקע הים", :refs ["Amos 9:3"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Reads Job 38:16 phrase as a remez to the sotah ritual: 'hidden from eyes' = suspected wife; 'floor of the sea' = dust and water test", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Enlarged letter ע in the word בקרקע signals the concealment-seeking 'eye' (עין) of adultery", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:27:24.011928122Z", :model "glm-5.2"}